    rdf:value """Wednesday, Jan. 29, 1908
I  Tatti. Warm. Rain
Giovanni dal Ponte
Drove Miss Alexander to town. She is waking up a bit, for she asked me what subject she should specialize upon. I suggested the whole Franciscan cycle in all of literature.
The  Serristori  had tea here, and Cust called — a prompt return! """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 51 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

